From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
X-Fasttrack-Source: claude
X-Fasttrack-Upstream: 06e3f54e8b22040ada01a28343badf1990b4dd7d
X-Fasttrack-CVE: CVE-2026-98558
X-Fasttrack-Backport: cve/CVE-2026-98558/6.1
From: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:51:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: flush skb_defer_nodes in dev_cpu_dead()

commit 06e3f54e8b22040ada01a28343badf1990b4dd7d upstream.

[ Backport: 6.1 has one defer list per softnet_data, not per-NUMA skb_defer_nodes. skb_defer_node_flush() takes a softnet_data ]
[ Backport: drop the per-node drain in dev_cpu_dead() and the CPU migration check; they protect per-node slots that 6.1 does not have ]
[ Backport: 6.1 has no kick_defer_list_purge(); reset defer_ipi_scheduled at the IPI call in skb_attempt_defer_free() ]

When a CPU goes offline, dev_cpu_dead() drains its softnet queues
(completion_queue, output_queue, poll_list, process_queue, and
input_pkt_queue), but leaves net_hotdata.skb_defer_nodes untouched.

If oldcpu goes offline while holding pending skbs in its
skb_defer_nodes lists (e.g. below the sysctl_skb_defer_max >> 1 IPI
threshold, or if the IPI races with CPU teardown), those skbs remain
stranded until oldcpu is brought back online. If any of these skbs
hold page_pool fragments, page_pool_destroy() will stall indefinitely
waiting for inflight pages to be returned when a netdev or driver is
torn down while oldcpu is offline.

Additionally, if smp_call_function_single_async() fails in
kick_defer_list_purge() because the target CPU went offline, reset
defer_ipi_scheduled to 0 so future IPI kicks are not blocked when the
CPU comes back online.

Also, if oldcpu was the last online CPU on its NUMA node, drain that
node's slot across all CPUs so no skbs deferred from that node remain
stranded on idle remote CPUs (or if the node itself is subsequently
offlined).

Finally, in skb_attempt_defer_free(), re-check cpu_online(cpu) and
whether the caller migrated CPUs after llist_add(), flushing the node
list if so, to close the preemption TOCTOU race against CPU/node
teardown.

Fixes: 68822bdf76f1 ("net: generalize skb freeing deferral to per-cpu lists")
Fixes: 5628f3fe3b16 ("net: add NUMA awareness to skb_attempt_defer_free()")
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/20260916003430.3612956-1-kris.pan@intel.com/
Signed-off-by: Eric Dumazet <edumazet@google.com>
Cc: Kris Pan <kris.pan@intel.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260923130318.607255-1-edumazet@google.com
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
---
 net/core/dev.c    | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 net/core/dev.h    |  3 +++
 net/core/skbuff.c | 11 +++++++++--
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/core/dev.c b/net/core/dev.c
index b2bef97ef4d1..e3bb05d1082f 100644
--- a/net/core/dev.c
+++ b/net/core/dev.c
@@ -6797,7 +6797,7 @@ static int napi_threaded_poll(void *data)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static void skb_defer_free_flush(struct softnet_data *sd)
+static void __skb_defer_free_flush(struct softnet_data *sd, int budget)
 {
 	struct sk_buff *skb, *next;
 	unsigned long flags;
@@ -6814,11 +6814,21 @@ static void skb_defer_free_flush(struct softnet_data *sd)
 
 	while (skb != NULL) {
 		next = skb->next;
-		napi_consume_skb(skb, 1);
+		napi_consume_skb(skb, budget);
 		skb = next;
 	}
 }
 
+void skb_defer_node_flush(struct softnet_data *sd)
+{
+	__skb_defer_free_flush(sd, 0);
+}
+
+static void skb_defer_free_flush(struct softnet_data *sd)
+{
+	__skb_defer_free_flush(sd, 1);
+}
+
 static __latent_entropy void net_rx_action(struct softirq_action *h)
 {
 	struct softnet_data *sd = this_cpu_ptr(&softnet_data);
@@ -11366,6 +11376,8 @@ static int dev_cpu_dead(unsigned int oldcpu)
 		input_queue_head_incr(oldsd);
 	}
 
+	skb_defer_node_flush(oldsd);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/net/core/dev.h b/net/core/dev.h
index c1e4a39c4078..06a7660c7128 100644
--- a/net/core/dev.h
+++ b/net/core/dev.h
@@ -122,4 +122,7 @@ static inline void netif_set_gro_max_size(struct net_device *dev,
 	WRITE_ONCE(dev->gro_max_size, size);
 }
 
+struct softnet_data;
+void skb_defer_node_flush(struct softnet_data *sd);
+
 #endif
diff --git a/net/core/skbuff.c b/net/core/skbuff.c
index a66066bc9861..211a34389f5c 100644
--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -6743,9 +6743,16 @@ nodefer:	__kfree_skb(skb);
 	WRITE_ONCE(sd->defer_list, skb);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&sd->defer_lock, flags);
 
+	if (unlikely(!cpu_online(cpu))) {
+		skb_defer_node_flush(sd);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	/* Make sure to trigger NET_RX_SOFTIRQ on the remote CPU
 	 * if we are unlucky enough (this seems very unlikely).
 	 */
-	if (unlikely(kick) && !cmpxchg(&sd->defer_ipi_scheduled, 0, 1))
-		smp_call_function_single_async(cpu, &sd->defer_csd);
+	if (unlikely(kick) && !cmpxchg(&sd->defer_ipi_scheduled, 0, 1)) {
+		if (smp_call_function_single_async(cpu, &sd->defer_csd))
+			WRITE_ONCE(sd->defer_ipi_scheduled, 0);
+	}
 }
